      <h3 id="web-platform">Corporate web platform migration</h3>
      <p class="work-meta" style="margin-bottom: .5rem">ConstructConnect · Product platform lead</p>
      <p>Worked on the redesign and migration of ConstructConnect.com to a multilingual (French and Spanish) Strapi headless CMS, without dedicated web engineering staff. Conversion protection was the main constraint: high-performing landing pages moved last, each against a parity benchmark, with A/B testing throughout. Accessibility and structured-data standards were set at the start rather than retrofitted.</p>

      <h3 id="help-center">Help center modernization</h3>
      <p class="work-meta" style="margin-bottom: .5rem">ConstructConnect · Project lead</p>
      <p>Help content ranged from fragmented to missing depending on which legacy product a user started in. I led the migration to Gainsight Customer Communities, set up tracking, front-end customization and UX standards, and added interactive product previews that let prospective customers try the experience before signing up. The aim was better-qualified leads and stronger progression from MQL to SQL.</p>

      <h3 id="aec-cares">AEC Cares nonprofit platform</h3>
      <p class="work-meta" style="margin-bottom: .5rem">AEC Cares · Web designer and developer</p>
      <p>Designed and built a HubSpot CMS site for a national Day-of-Service program, serving volunteers, administrators and donors with very different levels of technical comfort and device access. The CMS was structured so a small non-technical team could maintain it, a deliberate trade against editorial flexibility. Engagement, donations and mobile retention all improved after launch.</p>

      <h3 id="hill-farms">Hill Farms Neighborhood Association</h3>
      <p class="work-meta" style="margin-bottom: .5rem">Volunteer Technology Director · 2018 to present</p>
      <p>Card sorting with residents showed the site was organized around the association’s structure rather than what members came to do. I led a brand refresh and rebuilt the site on Google Cloud around member tasks. Event registrations and newsletter sign-ups went up after the relaunch.</p>
    </div>
